{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghw1rWL9NN3PqX8yUZ8a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Feo7MJK7MQ348o9QYkWt41","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 1489,1512p docs/API-INDEX.md; sed -n 1220,1255p docs/API-INDEX.md","description":"Read the mode7 and arcade module index entries"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1383,"cache_read_input_tokens":155203,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1383},"output_tokens":74,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37baaf64-6acc-44ac-b38d-1fce3a552962","uuid":"e0ef3ce2-ef44-47f0-bf24-de12000e6146","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:02:03.051Z","request_id":"req_011Cghw1rEDVbcAgemLiNSkm","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Feo7MJK7MQ348o9QYkWt41":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-060015__x4549c1/work/BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060015 && sed -n 1489,1512p docs/API-INDEX.md; sed -n 1220,1255p docs/API-INDEX.md","description":"Read the mode7 and arcade module index entries"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01Feo7MJK7MQ348o9QYkWt41":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-060015__x4549c1/work/BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060015"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Feo7MJK7MQ348o9QYkWt41","type":"tool_result","content":"## Module mode7: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance (engine/modules/mode7.js)\n\n- `new E.Mode7(o = {}) → mode7`: new E.Mode7({ floor, size, outside, wrap, sky, fog, far }): a Mode 7 view (the manual above)\n- `mode7.add(x, y, z, fn)`: gather a billboard: fn(g, sx, sy, k) draws it with its foot at (sx, sy), k screen pixels per unit\n- `mode7.begin(rect = {}, cam = this.cam)`: set up the projection for a camera (default this.cam) and a rectangle of the screen ({ W, H, x, y, cx, cy }: its size, its top left and its centre; focal: screen pixels per unit at a distance of one, instead of the fov)\n- `mode7.chase(b, o = {})`: the camera behind a body each step: back units behind it, h high, looking along its angle (o.angle to set one)\n- `mode7.draw(r, cam = this.cam)`: draw the view as an overlay over r's frame (in a split screen, r.viewport's part): sky, floor, fog, then the billboards far to near (gathered with add, rig, sprite; they are used up)\n- `mode7.drawFloor(g, vp)`: draw the floor below the horizon in the rectangle ({ x, y, w, h }), a row at a time, and the fog over it\n- `mode7.drawSky(g, r, vp)`: the sky above the horizon: a Backdrop turned with the heading, or a gradient of two colors\n- `mode7.fullRes(game, on)`: draw at the screen's own pixels (on, called each step: sharper, slower) or the game's again (off); returns the pixel size the game had (1 when it had no other)\n- `mode7.project(x, y, z = 0)`: a world point -> [screen x, screen y, screen pixels per unit there], or null at or behind the camera\n- `mode7.refresh()`: forget the floor's baked texture (after changing the map or the function: it bakes again)\n- `mode7.rig(rig, x, y, z = 0)`: gather a rig, drawn by the engine at the size its distance gives, from the camera's side (it faces rig.facing)\n- `mode7.rowDepth(sy)`: a screen row's floor distance ahead of the camera, or 0 at or above the horizon\n- `mode7.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: gather one of the engine's shapes (r.shape's: 'barrel', 'tree', ...; the full engine), seen from the camera's side at its distance's size: o.facing (radians), o.size (1)\n- `mode7.sprite(spr, x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: gather a sprite (E.sprite, or E.anim's frames at o.t, the game's time by default), its foot at the point: o.scale (world units a sprite pixel, 1), o.flip\n- `mode7.toFloor(sx, sy)`: a screen point -> the floor point under it [x, y], or null above the horizon\n- `mode7.view(k)`: the engine view a rig is drawn with at k pixels per unit, seen from the camera's heading (sixteenths, reused)\n- `mode7.cam`: the camera ({ x, y, h, angle, pitch, fov })\n- `mode7.horizon = 0`: the screen row of the horizon in the last drawing\n- `mode7.items = []`: the billboards gathered for the next draw\n- `mode7.o`: its options\n\n## Module physics: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through (engine/modules/physics.js)\n## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\n\n- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n- `arcade.add(points, at)`: add points to the player up (at: a world point { x, y, z } where they float up); an extra life at each threshold\n- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n- `arcade.card(text, seconds = 2)`: a card in the middle of the screen for seconds ('STAGE 2', 'PLAYER 2, READY!')\n- `arcade.carding`: is a card up? (hold play while it is)\n- `arcade.clear()`: take every card and word down\n- `arcade.coin()`: add a coin (credits on); returns the credits\n- `arcade.continue(seconds = 10, done)`: a continue: CONTINUE? counts down seconds; start, confirm or a tap continues (with the credits it takes): every player's lives back, the scores kept, done(true); at zero, done(false)\n- `arcade.continuing`: is the continue counting down?\n- `arcade.die()`: a life lost: 'again' (lives left), 'next' (the other player's turn) or 'over' (none left for anyone)\n- `arcade.draw(r, box)`: the frame over the game, after its drawing: the HUD (o.hud: 1UP, HI, 2UP in a row) along the top of box [x, y, w, h] (the playfield; the screen when none), the lives along its foot, the cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry\n- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\n- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\n- `arcade.enter(score, mode = '', done)`: open the initials entry for score; done(name) once it is taken and saved\n- `arcade.qualifies(score, mode = '')`: would score make the top ten (never in a demo)?\n- `arcade.say(text, seconds = 1.2)`: a short word under the cards for seconds ('READY!', 'EXTRA LIFE!')\n- `arcade.start(players = 1, o = {})`: begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them\n- `arcade.table(mode = '')`: the top ten of a mode: [{ name, score }]\n- `arcade.update(dt)`: a step: the cards count down, the entry and the continue read the keys\n- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\n- `arcade.credits`: coins in (null: free play)\n- `arcade.demo = false`: a demo is playing (no table)\n- `arcade.entry = null`: the initials being entered ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null\n- `arcade.game`: the game it serves\n- `arcade.hi = 0`: the high score shown\n- `arcade.id`: the game's name (its tables')\n- `arcade.mode = 'title'`: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'\n- `arcade.o`: the options\n- `arcade.p = null`: the player up\n- `arcade.phase = 'title'`: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' | 'scores'\n- `arcade.players = []`: [{ n, score, lives, save (the game's own: a stage kept while the other plays), next (the score of the next extra life) }]\n- `arcade.wheel = null`: where the letter wheel was last drawn (taps answer to it): { x, y, cw, up, down, ok } in screen pixels: three columns cw wide from x, the up and down bands [y0, y1], the OK button [x, y, w, h]\n\n## Module click: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an inventory (engine/modules/click.js)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37baaf64-6acc-44ac-b38d-1fce3a552962","uuid":"853810dc-bbe5-4279-a6b6-7b44c33fbd70","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:02:03.063Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Module mode7: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance (engine/modules/mode7.js)\n\n- `new E.Mode7(o = {}) → mode7`: new E.Mode7({ floor, size, outside, wrap, sky, fog, far }): a Mode 7 view (the manual above)\n- `mode7.add(x, y, z, fn)`: gather a billboard: fn(g, sx, sy, k) draws it with its foot at (sx, sy), k screen pixels per unit\n- `mode7.begin(rect = {}, cam = this.cam)`: set up the projection for a camera (default this.cam) and a rectangle of the screen ({ W, H, x, y, cx, cy }: its size, its top left and its centre; focal: screen pixels per unit at a distance of one, instead of the fov)\n- `mode7.chase(b, o = {})`: the camera behind a body each step: back units behind it, h high, look