{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi2ECx5ExBYbyvedjgJu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm finalizing the About/Credits content at the end, then moving on to the start file for game setup, settings, boot steps, scenes, deep links and `game.debug`.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6333,"cache_read_input_tokens":697014,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6333},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37baaf64-6acc-44ac-b38d-1fce3a552962","uuid":"0f39b284-2428-4dd7-b8a5-654b04aec1d8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:10:30.262Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi2ECfhPZ2FbNq9aGg11","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":2,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi2ECx5ExBYbyvedjgJu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0157wadrz8TCpcf1Vhvcbzqk","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-060015__x4549c1/work/BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060015/src/57-about.js","content":"/* =============================================================================\n * 57-about: the About/Credits pages (About, Source Information, Testing Feedback,\n * Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, Credits) and the credits roll's lines. The\n * same text is in the build's final reply and in exit-interview.json.\n * ========================================================================== */\nBZ.INFO = {\n  source: [\n    'Date: 2026-11-04 06:00:15',\n    'Source: Baseball (the sport), in the over-the-top arcade style.',\n    'Plan: PLAN.md',\n    'Genre and Perspective: Arcade sports (baseball) with a slapstick brawler mini-game (the Rhubarb) and a story Tour with light upgrades. Plate Cam: a Mode 7 view from behind the catcher for every pitch and swing; Broadcast Cam: a three-quarter ground view (pitch 52) of the park for fielding and running; Moonshot Cam: a Mode 7 chase of home runs; Replay Cam: the isometric view at half speed.',\n    'Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (full engine, every module: Mode 7, arcade, songs), with small changes (a bat weapon, mitts, four baseball hats, the PS face-button glyphs in the font, PlayStation symbols by default). Plain JavaScript, no libraries, bundled into one HTML file by a Node build script. AI Hub Session client 1.4.0. Tests: Node 24 (vm, headless engine) and Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium.',\n    'Art Direction: The engine\\'s native look: HD Humanoid rigs drawn as pixel art at res ps1 with expand, textured TileMap ballparks with baked mowing patterns, lit night games, particles. 40 new shape assets (bases, foul poles, light towers, scoreboards, the silo, a lighthouse, lava vents, habitats, tombstones, drones, the MEGA-TRON) and code-drawn sprites (the ball, reticles, glyph icons, the Batzooka).',\n    'Animation: The engine\\'s procedural rig system: new attack specs and poses for the contact and power swings, bunt, windup and pitch, throws, tags, dives, slides, wall climbs, umpire calls, celebrations and Rhubarb combos; a two-handed bat grip by IK. No motion-capture clips (the procedural fallback was used for every motion).',\n    'Audio: All in code with the engine\\'s chip synth: 20 original songs and stings in the engine\\'s notation (ballpark organ, surf rock, synthwave), about 60 sound effects, and Animalese-style babble voices for 15 characters (one syllable a letter, per-voice wave, pitch and rate). No audio files.',\n    'Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1-4 players: an online Derby round on a shared pitch sequence with ghost batters and home-run comets; client 1.4.0 pasted unmodified.',\n    'Testing: Headless tests in Node with the engine\\'s fixed-step game.advance and game.debug (one command, failures and a one-line count), CPU-vs-CPU balance sims, a scripted playthrough, Playwright browser checks with the engine\\'s check tool, screenshots for look, and the AI Hub harness.',\n    'Research: Read the engine handoff (README, API card, index lookups, asset card, mode7, arcade and Humanoid source) and the AI Hub protocol README and harness. No web research beyond those sources.',\n    'Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown',\n    'Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh',\n    'Usage: unknown'\n  ],\n  testing: [\n    'How many issues did testing catch? About 30 issues during the build.',\n    'How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? 7.',\n    'What was the most helpful test you ran? The seeded CPU-vs-CPU balance sim.',\n    'What was the least helpful test you ran? The asset-sheet lint of the new shapes.'\n  ],\n  engine: [\n    'What did you like most about the engine? Fixed-step headless play.',\n    'Did you get stuck or guess wrong? Yes, a few times.',\n    'What was the most important thing you had to build yourself? The baseball simulation.',\n    'What was the hardest part about using the engine? Floor rebakes at each zoom.',\n    'What did you change in the engine, and why? A bat, mitts, hats, glyphs.',\n    'If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be? Zoom-independent floor caching.'\n  ],\n  prompt: [\n    'What did you liked most about this prompt? A complete plan to build from.',\n    'What was confusing? Plan names and paths that differ from TASK.md.',\n    'What was the hardest thing to do? Fitting every system into one build.',\n    'What would you change in this prompt? Fewer, deeper systems.'\n  ]\n};\nBZ.ABOUT_PAGES = () => [\n  { title: 'ABOUT', logo: true, lines: ['An original over-the-top arcade baseball game. Pitch fireballs, swing a rocket-powered bat, rob homers off the wall, empty the benches in slapstick dust clouds, and save Kernel Field on a barnstorming tour.', 'Version ' + BZ.version + '  ·  engine ' + (E.versionLabel ? E.versionLabel() : E.version), 'Controls: stick/WASD/mouse aim · ✕/Space/click swing · □/J/right-click power · △/I bunt · R1/E Batzooka · Options/Esc pause.', 'Modes: Tour, Exhibition (1-4 players), Batzooka Derby, Spring Training. Online: AI Hub Derby rounds.'] },\n  { title: 'SOURCE INFORMATION', lines: BZ.INFO.source },\n  { title: 'TESTING FEEDBACK', lines: BZ.INFO.testing },\n  { title: 'ENGINE FEEDBACK', lines: BZ.INFO.engine },\n  { title: 'PROMPT FEEDBACK', lines: BZ.INFO.prompt },\n  { title: 'CREDITS', lines: ['Design, code, art, music and writing: Claude (Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh), built from PLAN.md.', 'Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (MIT License), github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.', 'Online: AI Hub Session client 1.4.0 (michaelcrosato/ai-hub).', 'Motion: procedural (the engine\\'s rig system). Asset sets: none beyond the engine\\'s core library.', 'All teams, players, parks and lines are original. No real players, teams or quotes.', 'Thanks for playing!'] }\n];\nBZ.CREDITS = () => ['BATZOOKA BASEBALL', '', 'THE KABOOM CUP IS HOME', '', 'DESIGN, CODE, ART, MUSIC, WRITING', 'Claude (Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, xhigh)', '', 'ENGINE', 'my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (MIT)', '', 'ONLINE', 'AI Hub Session client 1.4.0', '', 'STARRING', 'Dot \"Dynamite\" Delgado', 'Grandpa Ike Kowalski', 'Pep and Pip Porter', 'Moose Magnusson', 'Sunny Sato', 'Rosa \"Radar\" Reyes', 'Lefty Luna', 'Hank \"Hambone\" Hollis', 'Kid Kernel', '', 'THE RIVALS', 'Captain Bettina Brine', 'Iggy \"The Igniter\" Blaze', 'Commander Cosmo Vega', 'Count Rattlebones', 'ENFORCER-9000', '', 'IN THE BOOTH', 'Hap Harrigan', 'Big Lou Bombeck', 'Gloria Vox', 'Umpire Barb Hammersmith', '', 'AND', 'Mortimer Megamax, as himself', 'Popcorn Pete, as the mascot', '', 'NO BASEBALLS WERE HARMED.', 'A FEW JUMBOTRONS WERE.', '', 'THANKS FOR PLAYING!'];\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6333,"cache_read_input_tokens":697014,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6333},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37baaf64-6acc-44ac-b38d-1fce3a552962","uuid":"db608d00-42ef-448d-9b14-ed8d9987af54","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:10:55.140Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi2ECfhPZ2FbNq9aGg11","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0157wadrz8TCpcf1Vhvcbzqk":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-060015__x4549c1/work/BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060015/src/57-about.js","content":"/* =============================================================================\n * 57-about: the About/Credits pages (About, Source Information, Testing Feedback,\n * Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, Credits) and the credits roll's lines. The\n * same text is in the build's final reply and in exit-interview.json.\n * ========================================================================== */\nBZ.INFO = {\n  source: [\n    'Date: 2026-11-04 06:00:15',\n    'Source: Baseball (the sport), in the over-the-top arcade style.',\n    'Plan: PLAN.md',\n    'Genre and Perspective: Arcade sports (baseball) with a slapstick brawler mini-game (the Rhubarb) and a story Tour with light upgrades. Plate Cam: a Mode 7 view from behind the catcher for every pitch and swing; Broadcast Cam: a three-quarter ground view (pitch 52) of the park for fielding and running; Moonshot Cam: a Mode 7 chase of home runs; Replay Cam: the isometric view at half speed.',\n    'Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (full engine, every module: Mode 7, arcade, songs), with small changes (a bat weapon, mitts, four baseball hats, the PS face-button glyphs in the font, PlayStation symbols by default). Plain JavaScript, no libraries, bundled into one HTML file by a Node build script. AI Hub Session client 1.4.0. Tests: Node 24 (vm, headless engine) and Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium.',\n    'Art Direction: The engine\\'s native look: HD Humanoid rigs drawn as pixel art at res ps1 with expand, textured TileMap ballparks with baked mowing patterns, lit night games, particles. 40 new shape assets (bases, foul poles, light towers, scoreboards, the silo, a lighthouse, lava vents, habitats, tombstones, drones, the MEGA-TRON) and code-drawn sprites (the ball, reticles, glyph icons, the Batzooka).',\n    'Animation: The engine\\'s procedural rig system: new attack specs and poses for the contact and power swings, bunt, windup and pitch, throws, tags, dives, slides, wall climbs, umpire calls, celebrations and Rhubarb combos; a two-handed bat grip by IK. No motion-capture clips (the procedural fallback was used for every motion).',\n    'Audio: All in code with the engine\\'s chip synth: 20 original songs and stings in the engine\\'s notation (ballpark organ, surf rock, synthwave), about 60 sound effects, and Animalese-style babble voices for 15 characters (one syllable a letter, per-voice wave, pitch and rate). No audio files.',\n    'Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1-4 players: an online Derby round on a shared pitch sequence with ghost batters and home-run comets; client 1.4.0 pasted unmodified.',\n    'Testing: Headless tests in Node with the engine\\'s fixed-step game.advance and game.debug (one command, failures and a one-line count), CPU-vs-CPU balance sims, a scripted playthrough, Playwright browser checks with the engine\\'s check tool, screenshots for look, and the AI Hub harness.',\n    'Research: Read the engine handoff (README, API card, index lookups, asset card, mode7, arcade and Humanoid source) and the AI Hub protocol README and harness. No web research beyond those sources.',\n    'Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown',\n    'Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh',\n    'Usage: unknown'\n  ],\n  testing: [\n    'How many issues did testing catch? About 30 issues during the build.',\n    'How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? 7.',\n    'What was the most helpful test you ran? The seeded CPU-vs-CPU balance sim.',\n    'What was the least helpful test you ran? The asset-sheet lint of the new shapes.'\n  ],\n  engine: [\n    'What did you like most about the engine? Fixed-step headless play.',\n    'Did you get stuck or guess wrong? Yes, a few times.',\n    'What was the most important thing you had to build yourself? The baseball simulation.',\n    'What was the hardest part about using the engine? Floor rebakes at each zoom.',\n    'What did you change in the engine, and why? A bat, mitts, hats, glyphs.',\n    'If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be? Zoom-independent floor caching.'\n  ],\n  prompt: [\n    'What did you liked most about this prompt? A complete plan to build from.',\n    'What was confusing? Plan names and paths that differ from TASK.md.',\n    'What was the hardest thing to do? Fitting every system into one build.',\n    'What would you change in this prompt? Fewer, deeper systems.'\n  ]\n};\nBZ.ABOUT_PAGES = () => [\n  { title: 'ABOUT', logo: true, lines: ['An original over-the-top arcade baseball game. Pitch fireballs, swing a rocket-powered bat, rob homers off the wall, empty the benches in slapstick dust clouds, and save Kernel Field on a barnstorming tour.', 'Version ' + BZ.version + '  ·  engine ' + (E.versionLabel ? E.versionLabel() : E.version), 'Controls: stick/WASD/mouse aim · ✕/Space/click swing · □/J/right-click power · △/I bunt · R1/E Batzooka · Options/Esc pause.', 'Modes: Tour, Exhibition (1-4 players), Batzooka Derby, Spring Training. Online: AI Hub Derby rounds.'] },\n  { title: 'SOURCE INFORMATION', lines: BZ.INFO.source },\n  { title: 'TESTING FEEDBACK', lines: BZ.INFO.testing },\n  { title: 'ENGINE FEEDBACK', lines: BZ.INFO.engine },\n  { title: 'PROMPT FEEDBACK', lines: BZ.INFO.prompt },\n  { title: 'CREDITS', lines: ['Design, code, art, music and writing: Claude (Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh), built from PLAN.md.', 'Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (MIT License), github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.', 'Online: AI Hub Session client 1.4.0 (michaelcrosato/ai-hub).', 'Motion: procedural (the engine\\'s rig system). Asset sets: none beyond the engine\\'s core library.', 'All teams, players, parks and lines are original. No real players, teams or quotes.', 'Thanks for playing!'] }\n];\nBZ.CREDITS = () => ['BATZOOKA BASEBALL', '', 'THE KABOOM CUP IS HOME', '', 'DESIGN, CODE, ART, MUSIC, WRITING', 'Claude (Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, xhigh)', '', 'ENGINE', 'my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (MIT)', '', 'ONLINE', 'AI Hub Session client 1.4.0', '', 'STARRING', 'Dot \"Dynamite\" Delgado', 'Grandpa Ike Kowalski', 'Pep and Pip Porter', 'Moose Magnusson', 'Sunny Sato', 'Rosa \"Radar\" Reyes', 'Lefty Luna', 'Hank \"Hambone\" Hollis', 'Kid Kernel', '', 'THE RIVALS', 'Captain Bettina Brine', 'Iggy \"The Igniter\" Blaze', 'Commander Cosmo Vega', 'Count Rattlebones', 'ENFORCER-9000', '', 'IN THE BOOTH', 'Hap Harrigan', 'Big Lou Bombeck', 'Gloria Vox', 'Umpire Barb Hammersmith', '', 'AND', 'Mortimer Megamax, as himself', 'Popcorn Pete, as the mascot', '', 'NO BASEBALLS WERE HARMED.', 'A FEW JUMBOTRONS WERE.', '', 'THANKS FOR PLAYING!'];\n"}}}
