{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi416y2gYpiovQuZGK96","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"While the browser checks run, writing the dev-folder docs: ENGINE-CHANGES.md (every engine change and why), NOTES.md (decisions, deviations from the plan, tuning) and a README."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":415,"cache_read_input_tokens":831560,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":415},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37baaf64-6acc-44ac-b38d-1fce3a552962","uuid":"4e152c04-8c43-41ed-8029-e9fba3cbe898","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:33:59.831Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi416fRBUY9iVC8sjzhk"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi416y2gYpiovQuZGK96","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LYCnj5x1WVJi9yYzSecUkf","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-060015__x4549c1/work/BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060015/ENGINE-CHANGES.md","content":"# Engine changes (engine/my-3d2dge.js, from the my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff)\n\nEvery change is small and marked `BATZOOKA` in the source. Nothing else in the engine was edited.\n\n1. **`weapon: 'bat'` on `E.Humanoid`.** Added to the built-in weapon list (the warning check), a rest direction (the\n   bat up over the back shoulder), a draw branch in the HD style (a tapered capsule: knob, thin handle, thick barrel,\n   in `colors.bat`, optional `colors.batTape`) and in the classic style, and `tip()` returns the barrel's end (12 units).\n   Why: baseball needs a bat; a sword or staff reads wrong. The game adds the two-handed grip itself by wrapping\n   `rig.solvePose` (the documented hook) and the Batzooka overdraw on top.\n2. **`mitt` option** (`'fielder' | 'catcher' | 'first'`, with `mittHand: 'L' | 'R'`): a leather mitt drawn on the glove\n   hand in `colors.mitt`, rounder and bigger for the catcher. Why: fielders without gloves don't read as ballplayers.\n3. **Hats:** `hat: 'batting'` (a glossy helmet with a short brim and an ear flap on the side facing the pitcher:\n   `flap: -1 | 1`), `'mask'` (a catcher's or umpire's helmet worn backward with a three-bar cage), `'visor'` (a space\n   helmet: a dome with a tinted front, for the Moonbase Meteors) and `'tophat'` (a silk top hat with a `band`).\n   Portraits draw them too. Why: the uniforms and the cast need them.\n4. **Font glyphs:** ✕ ○ □ △ (so any `input.label()` text renders on a PlayStation pad), plus · … ✓ — ◂ ● ▲ ▼ used by\n   the game's text (the inning arrows, pips, check marks). Why: they drew as \"?\" before.\n5. **The standard `glyphs` setting** (Controller, \"Button symbols\"): default `'playstation'`, options PlayStation\n   (✕ ○ □ △) and Xbox (A B X Y). Why: TASK.md asks for PlayStation symbols on any pad with a Settings option for Xbox.\n\nNo engine bugs needed fixing. One engine behavior shaped the game: a TileMap's baked floor is cached per view\nscale, so a continuously zooming camera (`cam.frame` with a zoom range) re-bakes the floor every frame on a large\npark. The game zooms its Broadcast Cam in four discrete steps instead.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":415,"cache_read_input_tokens":831560,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":415},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37baaf64-6acc-44ac-b38d-1fce3a552962","uuid":"52eb588e-dbcd-4e07-be0c-308e1802bed2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:34:09.429Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi416fRBUY9iVC8sjzhk","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LYCnj5x1WVJi9yYzSecUkf":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-060015__x4549c1/work/BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-060015/ENGINE-CHANGES.md","content":"# Engine changes (engine/my-3d2dge.js, from the my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff)\n\nEvery change is small and marked `BATZOOKA` in the source. Nothing else in the engine was edited.\n\n1. **`weapon: 'bat'` on `E.Humanoid`.** Added to the built-in weapon list (the warning check), a rest direction (the\n   bat up over the back shoulder), a draw branch in the HD style (a tapered capsule: knob, thin handle, thick barrel,\n   in `colors.bat`, optional `colors.batTape`) and in the classic style, and `tip()` returns the barrel's end (12 units).\n   Why: baseball needs a bat; a sword or staff reads wrong. The game adds the two-handed grip itself by wrapping\n   `rig.solvePose` (the documented hook) and the Batzooka overdraw on top.\n2. **`mitt` option** (`'fielder' | 'catcher' | 'first'`, with `mittHand: 'L' | 'R'`): a leather mitt drawn on the glove\n   hand in `colors.mitt`, rounder and bigger for the catcher. Why: fielders without gloves don't read as ballplayers.\n3. **Hats:** `hat: 'batting'` (a glossy helmet with a short brim and an ear flap on the side facing the pitcher:\n   `flap: -1 | 1`), `'mask'` (a catcher's or umpire's helmet worn backward with a three-bar cage), `'visor'` (a space\n   helmet: a dome with a tinted front, for the Moonbase Meteors) and `'tophat'` (a silk top hat with a `band`).\n   Portraits draw them too. Why: the uniforms and the cast need them.\n4. **Font glyphs:** ✕ ○ □ △ (so any `input.label()` text renders on a PlayStation pad), plus · … ✓ — ◂ ● ▲ ▼ used by\n   the game's text (the inning arrows, pips, check marks). Why: they drew as \"?\" before.\n5. **The standard `glyphs` setting** (Controller, \"Button symbols\"): default `'playstation'`, options PlayStation\n   (✕ ○ □ △) and Xbox (A B X Y). Why: TASK.md asks for PlayStation symbols on any pad with a Settings option for Xbox.\n\nNo engine bugs needed fixing. One engine behavior shaped the game: a TileMap's baked floor is cached per view\nscale, so a continuously zooming camera (`cam.frame` with a zoom range) re-bakes the floor every frame on a large\npark. The game zooms its Broadcast Cam in four discrete steps instead.\n"}}}
